---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Brief = `We went out for dinner, six of us, and nobody can work out
what they owe. Ask me the bill, how many people, and what
tip we are leaving, and tell me what each person pays.`;

const Sample = `Bill total: 84.50 [Enter]
How many people? 6 [Enter]
Tip percent: 18 [Enter]

Each person pays: 16.62`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp-lua/unit-1/cc-set-1" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back to Set 1
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: Tip Split</h1>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Brief</h2>

          <Code
            code={Brief}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="What they asked for"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Write your requirements list before you write any code.</b> What
            goes in, what gets worked out, what comes out, and{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">every question the brief did not
            answer.</b>
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>Three things go in and one comes out. Get that working before you worry about anything else.</li>
            <li><b>Is the tip worked out on the whole bill or on each share?</b> The two give the same answer here. Say which one you did and why.</li>
            <li>Money has two decimal places and Lua does not know that. Decide what you are doing about it and write it down.</li>
            <li>Test it with a bill that does not divide evenly.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="success">
          <h2>Sample Output</h2>

          <Code
            code={Sample}
            frame="terminal"
            title="Sample Output"
            lang="txt"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-3">Your numbers will differ. <b>Run it three times</b> with different inputs and keep the outputs.</p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your requirements list and your program folder, named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">cc-tip-split</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
